	(text "THE WINDOW: READ LATCH, WRITE BUFFER, WRITE REQUEST; THE Y AND CONTROL REGISTERS" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 12.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "aa56c6b7-7e5c-5888-8bf8-4e0d8918f928"))
	(text "Memory-mapped; every decode is on TEXT (on the ribbon: WSEL = the window 7C00-7FFF, -WRY = a write to 7806,\n-WRCTL = a write to 7804, -RDMOUSE = a read of 7806). Reads: IC6 loads the CPU-half byte on each QC rise and drives\nD0-D7 while WSEL AND -MRD low (IC17B). Writes: WRQ (IC13A) = WSEL AND -MRW low (IC16A) at CHARCLOCK;\n-WE = NAND(WRQ, NMUX, WEPH, GWR) (IC17A) = counts 9-10, IC7 drives the RAM only then; RAM -OE off in that half.\nIC10: the Y register (7806). IC19: the control register (7804): TEXT-OFF (TEXT-ON to TEXT), GFX-ON, XOR, DPAGE,\nCPAGE, MOUSE-ON." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "68d7c86b-32b4-5921-a809-407e6ccbb367"))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
